,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124399","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124399","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124399.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124399.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"<!--\r\nPlease target the `master` branch. We will take care of backporting relevant fixes to older versions.\r\n\r\nBefore submitting, please read our checklist for contributors:\r\nhttps://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/development/engine/introduction.html#checklist-for-new-contributors\r\n\r\nUse of AI must be disclosed and should include a description of how it was used.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes [Proposal #15460](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/15460)\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\n<del>Adjusting `light_temperature` will directly set the `light_color` to the target color. But you can still manually adjust `light_color`.  </del>\r\n\r\n<del>This logic is different from the logic when `physical unit lights` is enabled, because in fact you can set a light's color to pure white when `physical unit lights` is disabled, but a color from temperature can't be pure white. So intuitively, there seems nothing wrong to me with this interaction method, but I feel there might be a better way🥲. I will modify if anyone can tell me a better way.</del>\r\n\r\n<img width=\"273\" height=\"65\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/21300140-ed19-4a7c-8a48-a95af9114abb\" />\r\n\r\nI apologize for hastily submitting this PR without having fully thought it through.\r\n\r\nI felt the previous implementation was unreasonable, so I modified it. Now whether to multiply the temperature color to the original color is decided by a toggle. This toggle will only be shown when `use_physical_light_units` is disabled in Project Settings. Now it behaves the same as when `use_physical_light_units` is enabled if you turn it on. \r\n\r\n<img width=\"470\" height=\"98\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8d708e49-2a0f-410a-af56-1cdb8edfa355\" />\r\n\r\n<img width=\"505\" height=\"119\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/01b7e124-07d5-45a5-aea2-43380f0c2087\" />\r\n\r\n<img width=\"488\" height=\"80\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2fb8193d-eba6-49ab-8c4e-e668aa72f3ef\" />\r\n\r\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124399/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":2,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124399/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}